1
00:00:01,251 --> 00:00:07,173
THIS PROGRAM CONTAINS AI-GENERATED CONTENT

2
00:00:07,174 --> 00:00:09,258
[panting]

3
00:00:09,259 --> 00:00:11,552
[♪ tense music playing]

4
00:00:11,553 --> 00:00:13,472
[door closes]

5
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:22,564
[hammer cocks]

6
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:38,038
[grunting]

7
00:00:50,217 --> 00:00:52,386
[breathing heavily]

8
00:01:09,152 --> 00:01:11,154
[♪ theme music playing]

9
00:01:14,908 --> 00:01:18,369
MURDER CLUB: LIAR'S TABLE

10
00:01:18,370 --> 00:01:20,037
Oh!

11
00:01:20,038 --> 00:01:23,000
You're the MASTER.

12
00:01:23,667 --> 00:01:24,668
Huh?

13
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:27,420
Who's the MASTER?

14
00:01:27,421 --> 00:01:29,131
- Aren't you the MASTER?
- My brother's the MASTER.

15
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:31,716
No. It's you, isn't it?

16
00:01:31,717 --> 00:01:33,217
- Me?
- [Mr. X] Yes.

17
00:01:33,218 --> 00:01:34,594
- I'm Mr. L.
- [Mr. X] Earlier,

18
00:01:34,595 --> 00:01:36,637
it said in the news article

19
00:01:36,638 --> 00:01:39,432
that one brother was taken to hospital
while the other fled.

20
00:01:39,433 --> 00:01:41,809
"Phone scam gang on the run
got into a car crash."

21
00:01:41,810 --> 00:01:43,853
"Technical mastermind seriously injured."

22
00:01:43,854 --> 00:01:47,148
I was involved in an accident

23
00:01:47,149 --> 00:01:49,526
where I injured my leg
while fleeing with my older brother.

24
00:01:50,736 --> 00:01:54,947
HE WAS LIMPING WHEN HE WENT IN
BUT HE WASN'T WHEN HE CAME OUT

25
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:57,158
[Mr. T] You're saying
he's actually the MASTER, not Mr. L?

26
00:01:57,159 --> 00:01:58,285
So Mr. L is the one who died?

27
00:01:58,869 --> 00:02:01,120
WERE THE MASTER AND MR. L TWINS?

28
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:03,122
- [Mr. T] But--
- Here's what we know.

29
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:05,708
- Mr. L should have a limp.
- [Mr. X] Right.

30
00:02:05,709 --> 00:02:08,210
But the person claiming
to be Mr. L right now

31
00:02:08,211 --> 00:02:09,962
is faking a limp.

32
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:12,715
He's living under the identity of Mr. L.

33
00:02:12,716 --> 00:02:15,885
One of my card clues
is a prison guard's testimony.

34
00:02:15,886 --> 00:02:19,513
It said, "I heard two men
raise their voices."

35
00:02:19,514 --> 00:02:21,515
- Two men were fighting.
- [Mr. X] Right.

36
00:02:21,516 --> 00:02:23,643
They fought as if they wanted
to kill each other.

37
00:02:23,644 --> 00:02:27,396
So I think the MASTER and Mr. L
fought over money,

38
00:02:27,397 --> 00:02:30,317
and their lives ended up switched.

39
00:02:30,901 --> 00:02:33,444
WHAT IS MR. L'S TRUE IDENTITY?

40
00:02:33,445 --> 00:02:35,446
[host] <i>It is time
for the private conversations.</i>

41
00:02:35,447 --> 00:02:38,866
We confirmed that we all
fired our guns at least once.

42
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:41,202
- I only fired once at the cabinet.
- [Mr. L] Right.

43
00:02:41,203 --> 00:02:43,579
So I can't be the culprit, can I?

44
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:45,331
- The gun…
- We can't be sure of that.

45
00:02:45,332 --> 00:02:47,459
Do you remember when you fired your gun?

46
00:02:48,043 --> 00:02:49,126
<i>It was at 00:25.</i>

47
00:02:49,127 --> 00:02:51,129
- [Mr. P] <i>Yeah, it was around that time.
- Okay.</i>

48
00:02:51,797 --> 00:02:53,839
- What was it you took?
- [Mr. L] Why'd you shoot it?

49
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:57,301
We impersonate prosecutors and tell people
to check their account, right?

50
00:02:57,302 --> 00:02:59,804
That phishing scam was my idea.

51
00:02:59,805 --> 00:03:01,055
- I came up with it.
- Yes.

52
00:03:01,056 --> 00:03:03,015
But we ran the scam so many times

53
00:03:03,016 --> 00:03:04,725
that clients started to catch on,

54
00:03:04,726 --> 00:03:06,061
so we needed a new idea.

55
00:03:06,687 --> 00:03:08,521
<i>The new ideas were in that cabinet.</i>

56
00:03:08,522 --> 00:03:10,898
New ideas? So you went to get the script--

57
00:03:10,899 --> 00:03:12,191
To show it to the MASTER.

58
00:03:12,192 --> 00:03:14,026
- [Mr. L] For the MASTER?
- While we escaped.

59
00:03:14,027 --> 00:03:15,653
You must be pleased.

60
00:03:15,654 --> 00:03:18,072
- [Mr. P] What?
- Never mind.

61
00:03:18,073 --> 00:03:21,242
Then when you eventually
got to the control tower--

62
00:03:21,243 --> 00:03:22,535
He was already dead.

63
00:03:22,536 --> 00:03:24,620
- [Mr. L] He was dead.
- Yeah, that's right,

64
00:03:24,621 --> 00:03:27,248
- when we were so close to escaping.
- [Mr. L] Yeah.

65
00:03:27,249 --> 00:03:30,584
- We need to find who betrayed the MASTER.
- That's right.

66
00:03:30,585 --> 00:03:32,920
- [Mr. X] I think--
- I think you're the traitor.

67
00:03:32,921 --> 00:03:34,130
- Me?
- [Mr. X] No, that would be

68
00:03:34,131 --> 00:03:35,714
- way too obvious.
- You think so?

69
00:03:35,715 --> 00:03:37,591
[Mr. X] Yeah, that would be too easy.

70
00:03:37,592 --> 00:03:39,093
I think it's Ms. H because--

71
00:03:39,094 --> 00:03:40,177
You think it's Ms. H?

72
00:03:40,178 --> 00:03:42,012
- [Mr. X] She really--
- It's not her.

73
00:03:42,013 --> 00:03:43,848
I spoke to her,
and she said she's innocent.

74
00:03:43,849 --> 00:03:47,685
She got a bit teary
and insisted it wasn't her.

75
00:03:47,686 --> 00:03:49,437
What's your blood type?

76
00:03:49,438 --> 00:03:51,897
- I'm type A, which means I'm very timid.
- [chuckles]

77
00:03:51,898 --> 00:03:53,482
I don't have the personality

78
00:03:53,483 --> 00:03:54,567
- to kill someone.
- Right?

79
00:03:54,568 --> 00:03:56,111
- Yeah.
- I'm type A, too.

80
00:03:56,695 --> 00:03:58,946
[Mr. X] That doesn't prove anything.

81
00:03:58,947 --> 00:04:00,573
Here's why I think it's Ms. H.

82
00:04:00,574 --> 00:04:04,035
She took the disk containing the VIP list
from the storage room.

83
00:04:04,703 --> 00:04:08,789
CCTV CLUE 1
MS. H TOOK THE BACKUP DISK FIRST

84
00:04:08,790 --> 00:04:11,750
She must have been planning
to do something with it.

85
00:04:11,751 --> 00:04:15,254
- She didn't need the MASTER anymore.
- [Mr. X] Also…

86
00:04:15,255 --> 00:04:16,881
I also think it's Ms. H

87
00:04:16,882 --> 00:04:19,008
because she raised her gun
outside the gate…

88
00:04:19,009 --> 00:04:20,510
- [Mr. X] Right.
-…but she didn't shoot.

89
00:04:21,094 --> 00:04:24,680
SHE POINTED HER GUN
TOWARD THE CONTROL TOWER

90
00:04:24,681 --> 00:04:27,099
When the gate opened soon after,

91
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:29,643
I think she went into the control tower
and fired her gun.

92
00:04:29,644 --> 00:04:31,645
- She didn't need the MASTER…
- Right.

93
00:04:31,646 --> 00:04:33,230
-…and got the disk--
- [Mr. L] She could put

94
00:04:33,231 --> 00:04:34,315
a new team together.

95
00:04:34,316 --> 00:04:36,484
And her younger brother
was scammed out of 150 million won,

96
00:04:36,485 --> 00:04:38,695
- which is a huge amount of money.
- It is.

97
00:04:39,613 --> 00:04:41,989
What do you think of Mr. T?
Right now, there's nothing…

98
00:04:41,990 --> 00:04:44,074
We barely have any clues about him.

99
00:04:44,075 --> 00:04:45,785
That makes him more dangerous.

100
00:04:45,786 --> 00:04:47,536
It's either Ms. H or Mr. T.

101
00:04:47,537 --> 00:04:49,622
It's one of those two.
We narrowed it down.

102
00:04:49,623 --> 00:04:52,291
But I don't think you should
jump to conclusions

103
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:54,126
because we've only been here five minutes,

104
00:04:54,127 --> 00:04:55,878
and you've already been swayed

105
00:04:55,879 --> 00:04:58,547
- into changing your mind. [laughing]
- That's my weakness.

106
00:04:58,548 --> 00:05:00,634
It sounds like
you might be on to something.

107
00:05:01,384 --> 00:05:02,677
That darn Ms. H!

108
00:05:04,262 --> 00:05:05,387
She's the culprit.

109
00:05:05,388 --> 00:05:09,850
To start with, I think Mr. L
is spewing nonsense.

110
00:05:09,851 --> 00:05:11,644
He's limping now,

111
00:05:11,645 --> 00:05:14,271
but we saw on the CCTV
that his leg was fine.

112
00:05:14,272 --> 00:05:16,607
- There is so much pointing at him.
- Way too much.

113
00:05:16,608 --> 00:05:18,984
I think he talked off the cuff earlier,

114
00:05:18,985 --> 00:05:20,987
not knowing so much evidence
would come out.

115
00:05:21,696 --> 00:05:25,574
Look, he's limping! His leg is hurting.

116
00:05:25,575 --> 00:05:26,784
My brother is actually the MASTER.

117
00:05:26,785 --> 00:05:28,035
I hung him up.

118
00:05:28,036 --> 00:05:30,329
There was a shot fired before.
I think that was me.

119
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:32,665
- And now, his lies are unraveling.
- [grunts]

120
00:05:32,666 --> 00:05:33,749
He's being inconsistent.

121
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:35,709
So he's becoming the prime suspect.

122
00:05:35,710 --> 00:05:38,671
<i>The person I suspect is Mr. L.</i>

123
00:05:38,672 --> 00:05:39,755
ROUND 3 CARD CLUES

124
00:05:39,756 --> 00:05:40,840
AI LOG, P'S NOTEBOOK, USB

125
00:05:40,841 --> 00:05:42,424
MASTER'S TORN-UP NOTE,
PRISON VISITATION LOG

126
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:45,886
[host] <i>The fourth shared clue
is the Goldilocks Zone.</i>

127
00:05:45,887 --> 00:05:47,304
[Ms. H] Goldilocks? What's that?

128
00:05:47,305 --> 00:05:48,973
[host] <i>The Goldilocks Zone</i>

129
00:05:48,974 --> 00:05:54,062
<i>is the ideal shooting distance,
not too close, not too far.</i>

130
00:05:54,896 --> 00:05:58,816
That means someone in this zone
fired the fatal shot.

131
00:05:58,817 --> 00:06:00,360
It's the viable range.

132
00:06:00,861 --> 00:06:02,778
[Mr. T] Shall we take
a card clue from Mr. P?

133
00:06:02,779 --> 00:06:05,489
- [Ms. H] Yes.
- We already have proof that it's not me.

134
00:06:05,490 --> 00:06:06,740
I fired once at the cabinet.

135
00:06:06,741 --> 00:06:08,326
- I'll take from one Mr. T.
- Okay.

136
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:10,244
MR. X TAKES ONE FROM MR. T

137
00:06:10,245 --> 00:06:12,413
MR. T'S CARDS ARE SUDDENLY VERY POPULAR

138
00:06:12,414 --> 00:06:14,623
- [Mr. T] There's evidence we missed.
- [Mr. L] Oh, yeah.

139
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:16,167
I really hope we find
something conclusive.

140
00:06:20,255 --> 00:06:21,338
OBJECT CLUES COLLECTED

141
00:06:21,339 --> 00:06:22,423
[Mr. T] Hey, look.

142
00:06:22,424 --> 00:06:24,550
Mr. L keeps pretending to limp.

143
00:06:24,551 --> 00:06:26,010
You don't need to do that.

144
00:06:26,011 --> 00:06:28,596
- How rude to an injured person.
- [Mr. T] You don't need to fake it.

145
00:06:28,597 --> 00:06:31,348
[Mr. P] It says here the system owner,

146
00:06:31,349 --> 00:06:33,351
the server administrator,

147
00:06:33,852 --> 00:06:36,187
changed from the MASTER to Mr. L.

148
00:06:36,771 --> 00:06:39,940
THE MASTER WAS BLOCKED FROM THE SERVER

149
00:06:39,941 --> 00:06:41,985
MASTER: ACCESS DENIED

150
00:06:42,819 --> 00:06:45,530
I'll come clean. I'm not Mr. L.
I'm actually the MASTER.

151
00:06:46,197 --> 00:06:48,699
- [grunts]
- So the MASTER isn't dead yet.

152
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:50,160
The one who died is Mr. L.

153
00:06:50,744 --> 00:06:55,998
THE MASTER WAS PRETENDING
TO BE HIS TWIN BROTHER MR. L

154
00:06:55,999 --> 00:06:59,084
MASTER

155
00:06:59,085 --> 00:07:01,879
It's been really hard
pretending to be Mr. L.

156
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,297
I am actually the MASTER.

157
00:07:03,298 --> 00:07:05,591
- What the heck?
- [Mr. X] The victim was Mr. L, right?

158
00:07:05,592 --> 00:07:08,302
I'm the MASTER,
and my dead younger brother

159
00:07:08,303 --> 00:07:09,970
is still hanging in the control tower.

160
00:07:09,971 --> 00:07:11,348
- Who hung him?
- I must find the killer.

161
00:07:11,931 --> 00:07:14,516
I hung him up,
but I'm not the one who killed him.

162
00:07:14,517 --> 00:07:16,393
- [Mr. X] You sound like real siblings.
- [laughing]

163
00:07:16,394 --> 00:07:18,103
HEHE

164
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:20,522
- Unbelievable!
- [laughing]

165
00:07:20,523 --> 00:07:22,066
Who are you really? Darn it.

166
00:07:22,067 --> 00:07:23,734
You would lose, Mr. P.

167
00:07:23,735 --> 00:07:26,362
He's got fast reflexes,
so you can't beat him.

168
00:07:26,363 --> 00:07:27,863
So you're the MASTER, not Mr. L?

169
00:07:27,864 --> 00:07:30,949
Yes, I'm the MASTER,
which just proves I'm not the culprit

170
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:32,451
because my brother was essential to me.

171
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:35,704
What kind of scary person hangs up
and shoots an essential person?

172
00:07:35,705 --> 00:07:36,914
[the MASTER] I'll explain the story.

173
00:07:36,915 --> 00:07:38,791
Hear me out.

174
00:07:38,792 --> 00:07:39,793
Don't tear up.

175
00:07:40,585 --> 00:07:41,835
WAHH

176
00:07:41,836 --> 00:07:43,380
- [all laughing]
- [Mr. P] Don't put on a show!

177
00:07:43,963 --> 00:07:45,506
DISPLEASED

178
00:07:45,507 --> 00:07:47,800
You mustn't attack him.
You'll face consequences.

179
00:07:47,801 --> 00:07:49,802
- Who cares!
- He has fans around the world.

180
00:07:49,803 --> 00:07:50,970
We need to catch the culprit!

181
00:07:51,638 --> 00:07:53,639
My younger brother tried to kill me

182
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:55,599
because he was unhappy with his share.

183
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:58,602
So I had no choice but to restrain him…

184
00:07:58,603 --> 00:08:01,855
[voice cracking] …and the server…

185
00:08:01,856 --> 00:08:03,941
- [Mr. P] Why did your voice just crack?
- [Ms. H] Hey!

186
00:08:03,942 --> 00:08:06,527
- [laughing]
- [exclaiming]

187
00:08:06,528 --> 00:08:08,112
[Mr. T] You'll both get into trouble!

188
00:08:08,113 --> 00:08:09,363
We're all in for it.

189
00:08:09,364 --> 00:08:11,156
- We have to be careful.
- [Ms. H] Mr. L.

190
00:08:11,157 --> 00:08:12,574
We wouldn't tease Faker like this.

191
00:08:12,575 --> 00:08:14,576
I needed my brother to manage the system,

192
00:08:14,577 --> 00:08:16,453
and there was a chance
I might fail to retrieve

193
00:08:16,454 --> 00:08:18,038
the backup disk from the storage room.

194
00:08:18,039 --> 00:08:20,249
So I had no reason to kill my brother.

195
00:08:20,250 --> 00:08:22,543
I hung him up
and went to the storage room,

196
00:08:22,544 --> 00:08:24,962
and I came back at around 00:36,

197
00:08:24,963 --> 00:08:26,589
but he was already dead.

198
00:08:27,090 --> 00:08:28,173
CASE TIMELINE

199
00:08:28,174 --> 00:08:30,050
THE MASTER RETURNED AT 00:36

200
00:08:30,051 --> 00:08:31,969
I looked for the backup disk but--

201
00:08:31,970 --> 00:08:33,971
It wasn't there,
and it turns out she took it.

202
00:08:33,972 --> 00:08:35,765
- [the MASTER] Yeah.
- [Mr. X] Why did you take it?

203
00:08:36,349 --> 00:08:39,685
MS. H TOOK THE BACKUP DISK
FROM THE STORAGE ROOM AT 00:10

204
00:08:39,686 --> 00:08:40,978
Now, it's my turn to explain.

205
00:08:40,979 --> 00:08:42,438
I had a plan.

206
00:08:42,439 --> 00:08:44,440
After the escape, I planned to set up

207
00:08:44,441 --> 00:08:45,899
a two-person company with the MASTER

208
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:47,401
and take all of the profit.

209
00:08:47,402 --> 00:08:48,944
Just you two? You planned to ditch us?

210
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:50,863
- I'm sorry, but--
- [Mr. T] Hang on.

211
00:08:50,864 --> 00:08:52,448
What about everything we've done together?

212
00:08:52,449 --> 00:08:54,200
Were we used and tossed?

213
00:08:54,784 --> 00:08:56,828
- That reminds me of my wife.
- [laughing]

214
00:08:57,412 --> 00:08:59,121
CRACKING UP

215
00:08:59,122 --> 00:09:00,539
My goal was

216
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:02,082
to steal the backup disk

217
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:04,501
and use the VIP list on it

218
00:09:04,502 --> 00:09:07,380
to found a new organization of my own.

219
00:09:07,881 --> 00:09:09,256
<i>I wanted to be queen.</i>

220
00:09:09,257 --> 00:09:12,885
SHE AIMED TO BECOME THE BOSS
OF A NEW CRIME NETWORK

221
00:09:12,886 --> 00:09:14,970
I have another CCTV password.
Should we check it?

222
00:09:14,971 --> 00:09:16,430
- I have one too.
- Let's go check.

223
00:09:16,431 --> 00:09:17,807
I feel like we'll find something.

224
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:22,603
- [Mr. P] <i>What's this?
-</i> [Mr. X] <i>It's the younger brother!</i>

225
00:09:22,604 --> 00:09:24,147
- [Ms. H] <i>What?
-</i> [Mr. P] <i>The younger brother.</i>

226
00:09:24,731 --> 00:09:25,774
Mr. L!

227
00:09:26,858 --> 00:09:28,693
[Mr. P] <i>Yeah, that's Mr. L, right?</i>

228
00:09:29,444 --> 00:09:30,694
Who is that?

229
00:09:30,695 --> 00:09:32,279
- He's my brother.
- It's Mr. L.

230
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:34,782
It's Mr. L, who we mistook for the MASTER.

231
00:09:34,783 --> 00:09:36,451
- [Mr. P] <i>His hands are cuffed.
-</i> [Mr. T] <i>The time was 00:20.</i>

232
00:09:37,494 --> 00:09:41,081
CASE TIMELINE
MR. L WAS ALIVE AT 00:20

233
00:09:41,706 --> 00:09:43,415
CHECKING THE NEXT CCTV CLUE

234
00:09:43,416 --> 00:09:45,876
- [Ms. H] Oh, my.
- What? This is…

235
00:09:45,877 --> 00:09:47,128
- Who is that? Mr. X?
- Who's that?

236
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:53,300
MR. X IS LOOKING AT THE BODY

237
00:09:53,301 --> 00:09:54,718
- It's Mr. X.
- Mr. X!

238
00:09:54,719 --> 00:09:55,886
- Why is that me?
- He's still alive.

