471
00:18:39,035 --> 00:18:40,410
[Mr. T] That's just my opinion.

472
00:18:40,411 --> 00:18:41,494
ROUND 4 CARD CLUES

473
00:18:41,495 --> 00:18:42,912
SERVER SYSTEM LOG, VOICEMAIL,
APPEAL DISMISSAL

474
00:18:42,913 --> 00:18:44,247
COURT JUDGMENT,
MATERIALS STORED IN CABINET

475
00:18:44,248 --> 00:18:46,583
[host] <i>The final shared clue</i>

476
00:18:46,584 --> 00:18:49,169
<i>is the control tower
glass fragment analysis report.</i>

477
00:18:49,170 --> 00:18:50,795
[Mr. T] <i>So the glass was bulletproof.</i>

478
00:18:50,796 --> 00:18:53,965
The Goldilocks Zone
is between 25 m to 50 m.

479
00:18:53,966 --> 00:18:55,592
If the MASTER was shot to death,

480
00:18:55,593 --> 00:18:59,471
it had to be one of the two bullets
that were fired at 00:30.

481
00:18:59,472 --> 00:19:01,890
- One of the two.
- Then it had to be Mr. T or Ms. H

482
00:19:01,891 --> 00:19:03,725
- if it was 00:30.
- Let me just say this.

483
00:19:03,726 --> 00:19:07,270
As I tried to explain
before we got this clue,

484
00:19:07,271 --> 00:19:09,272
I'm certain Ms. H is the culprit.

485
00:19:09,273 --> 00:19:12,484
- Why?
- [Mr. T] She lied about her gunshot.

486
00:19:12,485 --> 00:19:15,945
We've now established
that Mr. L died at around 00:30.

487
00:19:15,946 --> 00:19:17,614
We're the two people
who fired at that time.

488
00:19:17,615 --> 00:19:18,949
But my bullet missed the mark,

489
00:19:19,575 --> 00:19:20,659
so that leaves Ms. H.

490
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:23,787
- But my file says I shot into the air too.
- You're lying.

491
00:19:23,788 --> 00:19:25,955
What if there was a surprising twist?

492
00:19:25,956 --> 00:19:27,832
The MASTER tied him up, right?

493
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:29,167
- [Ms. H] Yeah.
- After injuring him.

494
00:19:29,168 --> 00:19:31,586
What if Mr. P sprinted
to the control tower,

495
00:19:31,587 --> 00:19:34,547
flung the door open,
and beat him to death with his fists?

496
00:19:34,548 --> 00:19:37,467
Who, me?
Did you bump your head or something?

497
00:19:37,468 --> 00:19:39,386
- Couldn't that be it?
- [Mr. T] We saw earlier--

498
00:19:39,387 --> 00:19:42,013
It says he was shot to death.
What are you on about fists?

499
00:19:42,014 --> 00:19:43,306
Where did you shoot from, Ms. H?

500
00:19:43,307 --> 00:19:45,558
I'm a bit baffled
because it doesn't say here

501
00:19:45,559 --> 00:19:46,643
that I shot anyone.

502
00:19:46,644 --> 00:19:47,977
It says I shot into the air.

503
00:19:47,978 --> 00:19:50,021
Well, we can't check your file
to see if that's true…

504
00:19:50,022 --> 00:19:51,356
- Right.
-…so we can't believe you.

505
00:19:51,357 --> 00:19:54,693
I'm just surprised we suddenly
narrowed it down to two suspects.

506
00:19:54,694 --> 00:19:56,069
It's just my opinion.

507
00:19:56,070 --> 00:19:59,030
Why don't the three of us
just go over there and drink coffee

508
00:19:59,031 --> 00:20:00,532
while the two of you reach a compromise.

509
00:20:00,533 --> 00:20:02,367
Or just play rock paper scissors.

510
00:20:02,368 --> 00:20:04,244
I'm not willing to compromise

511
00:20:04,245 --> 00:20:05,579
because I'm certain it's Ms. H.

512
00:20:06,622 --> 00:20:09,874
IS THE CULPRIT MR. T OR MS. H?

513
00:20:09,875 --> 00:20:11,209
Why did you kill him, Ms. H?

514
00:20:11,210 --> 00:20:12,794
How will you make money after you escape?

515
00:20:12,795 --> 00:20:14,337
I think it was Mr. T.

516
00:20:14,338 --> 00:20:17,424
- We're in the same situation.
- Why did you kill him? Why did you lie?

517
00:20:17,425 --> 00:20:18,758
This doesn't make any sense.

518
00:20:18,759 --> 00:20:20,969
Why am I the one under suspicion?

519
00:20:20,970 --> 00:20:23,680
- That's just how life is.
- [Mr. T laughing]

520
00:20:23,681 --> 00:20:26,057
- It can be unfair and frustrating.
- [Ms. H] But we--

521
00:20:26,058 --> 00:20:27,934
I didn't expect this from you, Ms. H.

522
00:20:27,935 --> 00:20:29,978
Let's leave the case unresolved

523
00:20:29,979 --> 00:20:31,229
and go get dinner.

524
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:32,689
IS THIS HOW IT ENDS?

525
00:20:32,690 --> 00:20:34,107
- No one's owning up.
- [Ms. H] This is hard.

526
00:20:34,108 --> 00:20:36,025
- Shall we vote on the menu?
- Sure. What should we eat?

527
00:20:36,026 --> 00:20:37,737
- Pork belly!
- [Ms. H] Pork belly, of course.

528
00:20:38,612 --> 00:20:40,530
At 00:35, Mr. X and I

529
00:20:40,531 --> 00:20:42,574
faced each other at gunpoint.

530
00:20:42,575 --> 00:20:44,659
- [Mr. X] Inside the control tower.
- When was this?

531
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:45,827
- [Ms. H] At 00:35.
- In the control tower?

532
00:20:45,828 --> 00:20:47,245
- Why?
- This is new information.

533
00:20:47,246 --> 00:20:48,329
- So I--
- I'll explain.

534
00:20:48,330 --> 00:20:51,541
It says here
I arrived first at 00:32, right?

535
00:20:51,542 --> 00:20:53,835
<i>I saw that the MASTER was dead</i>

536
00:20:53,836 --> 00:20:55,503
<i>-and realized there was a traitor…</i>
- [gasps]

537
00:20:55,504 --> 00:20:57,756
…so I pulled my gun out
and stood on guard.

538
00:20:57,757 --> 00:20:59,424
That's when Ms. H suddenly appeared.

539
00:20:59,425 --> 00:21:00,801
So I was like, "What the heck?"

540
00:21:01,886 --> 00:21:04,096
"I'm going to shoot!"
That's what happened.

541
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:08,725
MR. X AND MS. H HAD A STANDOFF
IN THE CONTROL TOWER AT 00:35

542
00:21:08,726 --> 00:21:10,894
CASE TIMELINE
MS. H ARRIVED AT 00:35

543
00:21:10,895 --> 00:21:13,104
Tell us what you were doing
between 00:25 and 00:35.

544
00:21:13,105 --> 00:21:14,397
- Yeah, tell us again.
- Sure.

545
00:21:14,398 --> 00:21:16,775
- Then can we hear everyone's alibis?
- You go first.

546
00:21:16,776 --> 00:21:19,360
I'll tell you in detail.

547
00:21:19,361 --> 00:21:23,072
<i>I headed to the showers at 00:15.</i>

548
00:21:23,073 --> 00:21:26,493
I heard the second round
of gunshots at 00:21.

549
00:21:26,494 --> 00:21:28,578
- That was me.
- [Mr. T] It was Mr. X firing four times.

550
00:21:28,579 --> 00:21:31,039
Between 00:21 and 00:23…

551
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:33,833
- [Mr. X] <i>You were doing the math?
-</i> [Mr. T] <i>Yes, I was looking at the note</i>

552
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:35,585
<i>and I did take a shot</i>

553
00:21:35,586 --> 00:21:37,629
- from what is the Goldilocks Zone.
- [Mr. X] Okay.

554
00:21:37,630 --> 00:21:39,214
I did pull the trigger.

555
00:21:39,215 --> 00:21:42,091
But as I said earlier, needing a formula

556
00:21:42,092 --> 00:21:43,760
as I'm such a lousy shot, I missed.

557
00:21:43,761 --> 00:21:46,596
As soon as I fired,
I heard another gunshot.

558
00:21:46,597 --> 00:21:49,015
I'm assuming it was Ms. H's gun.

559
00:21:49,016 --> 00:21:52,352
I arrived at the control tower at 00:45.

560
00:21:52,353 --> 00:21:54,562
Three people were already there.

561
00:21:54,563 --> 00:21:56,105
There were three people at 00:45.

562
00:21:56,106 --> 00:21:57,315
That must have been me and--

563
00:21:57,316 --> 00:21:59,275
Me and Ms. H.

564
00:21:59,276 --> 00:22:02,904
CASE TIMELINE
MR. T ARRIVED AT 00:45

565
00:22:02,905 --> 00:22:05,156
When did you arrive, Mr. P?

566
00:22:05,157 --> 00:22:06,407
Good question.

567
00:22:06,408 --> 00:22:07,492
Walk us through--

568
00:22:07,493 --> 00:22:08,744
Don't flash your file around.

569
00:22:09,745 --> 00:22:11,913
A MAN WITHOUT ANY SECRETS

570
00:22:11,914 --> 00:22:13,791
[Mr. P] <i>I got there at 00:55.</i>

571
00:22:14,583 --> 00:22:17,001
Four people were there already.

572
00:22:17,002 --> 00:22:19,838
- [Mr. T] So you were the last to arrive.
- Yeah, I got there last.

573
00:22:19,839 --> 00:22:24,384
It took me 32 minutes
to circle the entire prison.

574
00:22:24,385 --> 00:22:28,721
So what on earth were you doing
that it took you 55 minutes?

575
00:22:28,722 --> 00:22:29,807
Oh, yeah.

576
00:22:30,474 --> 00:22:33,393
I'm not one to run
even if I'm in a real hurry.

577
00:22:33,394 --> 00:22:35,436
Oh, you walked?

578
00:22:35,437 --> 00:22:37,605
I'm a country boy.

579
00:22:37,606 --> 00:22:40,109
So even when the clock is ticking,
I move at a leisurely pace.

580
00:22:41,235 --> 00:22:43,696
HE HAD TO COLLECT
THE INVESTIGATION RECORDS

581
00:22:44,280 --> 00:22:45,364
AND NEEDED TO TAKE DOWN ALL THE MEMBERS

582
00:22:45,948 --> 00:22:49,450
SO HE ARRIVED AT THE CONTROL TOWER LAST

583
00:22:49,451 --> 00:22:52,328
There's a note
that I didn't disclose before.

584
00:22:52,329 --> 00:22:53,955
This is Mr. X's mobile phone.

585
00:22:53,956 --> 00:22:56,416
It shows he held
a grudge against the boss.

586
00:22:56,417 --> 00:22:58,001
<i>I think you should all take a look.</i>

587
00:22:58,002 --> 00:23:00,712
- [Mr. T] <i>He has motive too.
-</i> [Ms. H] <i>Yes, a very clear motive.</i>

588
00:23:00,713 --> 00:23:03,214
- But the motive doesn't matter.
- [the MASTER] He's right.

589
00:23:03,215 --> 00:23:05,508
- We all had a reasonable motive.
- [Ms. H] Yeah.

590
00:23:05,509 --> 00:23:07,594
- What matters is our whereabouts at 00:30.
- [Mr. T] Yeah.

591
00:23:07,595 --> 00:23:09,512
We need to find the killer,

592
00:23:09,513 --> 00:23:10,597
and he died at 00:30…

593
00:23:10,598 --> 00:23:12,640
00:30 is right, isn't it?

594
00:23:12,641 --> 00:23:13,933
That's when Mr. L died.

595
00:23:13,934 --> 00:23:16,477
<i>We all believe he fired
those four shots, right?</i>

596
00:23:16,478 --> 00:23:18,396
So we can strike Mr. X off the list.

597
00:23:18,397 --> 00:23:20,523
As for Mr. P and the MASTER,

598
00:23:20,524 --> 00:23:24,444
<i>we saw proof that the MASTER
saw Mr. L alive before 00:30,</i>

599
00:23:24,445 --> 00:23:26,780
<i>and there's physical evidence
proving Mr. P's alibi.</i>

600
00:23:27,573 --> 00:23:31,367
So our focus should be
on whether the victim

601
00:23:31,368 --> 00:23:33,578
was shot by me or Ms. H.

602
00:23:33,579 --> 00:23:37,707
It had to be one our bullets.
It's the only explanation.

603
00:23:37,708 --> 00:23:39,752
But that's only if he was
shot from the outside.

604
00:23:40,336 --> 00:23:42,420
What? He was shot from inside the tower?

605
00:23:42,421 --> 00:23:46,466
I think whoever shot him
would have left and come back later,

606
00:23:46,467 --> 00:23:49,469
- as if it was their first time entering.
- Exactly.

607
00:23:49,470 --> 00:23:52,096
It's like when you play <i>Among Us</i>,
you kill then run like hell.

608
00:23:52,097 --> 00:23:55,558
I agree. Someone lied earlier.

609
00:23:55,559 --> 00:23:58,519
They went to the control tower twice
and killed Mr. L the first time.

610
00:23:58,520 --> 00:23:59,771
[Mr. P] Yes, it's from the inside.

611
00:23:59,772 --> 00:24:03,024
So someone shot him at 00:30,
left the tower, then returned at 00:45?

612
00:24:03,025 --> 00:24:04,609
That's the most likely…

613
00:24:04,610 --> 00:24:06,736
I think that would be
too difficult to pull off.

614
00:24:06,737 --> 00:24:09,739
What's difficult about it?
Shoot, leave, and come back in.

615
00:24:09,740 --> 00:24:12,450
Who do you think is guilty, Mr. L?

616
00:24:12,451 --> 00:24:14,787
I think Mr. X.

617
00:24:15,996 --> 00:24:18,122
To start with, Mr. X found the body first.

618
00:24:18,123 --> 00:24:20,458
- Why are you suddenly accusing Mr. X?
- [Mr. T] It can't be Mr. X.

619
00:24:20,459 --> 00:24:21,876
I think it is Mr. X.

620
00:24:21,877 --> 00:24:24,212
- You said you had a standoff.
- [Mr. X] Yeah.

621
00:24:24,213 --> 00:24:26,548
[the MASTER] The person who was
in the tower at 00:30 was Mr. X.

622
00:24:27,049 --> 00:24:28,592
Why did you do it, Mr. X?

623
00:24:29,468 --> 00:24:30,551
I didn't.

624
00:24:30,552 --> 00:24:31,844
He says it's not him, so there you go.

625
00:24:31,845 --> 00:24:34,305
The fact that he fired so many shots
and where they landed--

626
00:24:34,306 --> 00:24:35,974
The consecutive shots are a lie?

627
00:24:35,975 --> 00:24:40,144
The evidence points to four rapid shots,
but it doesn't sit right with me.

628
00:24:40,145 --> 00:24:42,772
I think he fired those four shots
to shake off suspicion

629
00:24:42,773 --> 00:24:44,232
and used another gun to…

630
00:24:44,233 --> 00:24:46,359
The fact that he is
bringing up another gun…

631
00:24:46,360 --> 00:24:49,195
- He went to find another gun.
-…suggests that Mr. L…

632
00:24:49,196 --> 00:24:50,655
No, the MASTER had another gun.

633
00:24:50,656 --> 00:24:52,115
[Mr. T] Let me just say this.

634
00:24:52,116 --> 00:24:55,702
If he had used another gun,
we'd have found evidence

635
00:24:55,703 --> 00:24:59,956
proving there was another gun
with X amount of bullets remaining.

636
00:24:59,957 --> 00:25:01,874
But there's no such evidence,

637
00:25:01,875 --> 00:25:03,584
so I think we can dismiss that theory.

638
00:25:03,585 --> 00:25:07,463
What matters most right now
is the direction you shot from.

639
00:25:07,464 --> 00:25:11,092
If we can't determine the direction
Mr. X was shooting from,

640
00:25:11,093 --> 00:25:13,428
the most plausible scenario
is that Ms. H is lying.

641
00:25:13,429 --> 00:25:16,098
- [Mr. X] Can I share my theory?
- But I'm not lying.

642
00:25:16,598 --> 00:25:18,224
Mr. T and I have the exact same alibis,

643
00:25:18,225 --> 00:25:19,809
but he keeps accusing me.

644
00:25:19,810 --> 00:25:21,269
So I think it's him

645
00:25:21,270 --> 00:25:24,063
since he keeps trying to pin it on me.

646
00:25:24,064 --> 00:25:27,734
It's a very risky move
to rule out everyone else

647
00:25:27,735 --> 00:25:29,944
and say that it can't be me,
so it must be them.

648
00:25:29,945 --> 00:25:32,113
To everyone else,
it's a fifty-fifty toss-up.

649
00:25:32,114 --> 00:25:34,699
So I made a big gamble.

650
00:25:34,700 --> 00:25:37,076
If the shot was fired inside,
we would have heard it.

651
00:25:37,077 --> 00:25:39,579
But we heard all the gunshots,

652
00:25:39,580 --> 00:25:42,540
and the CCTV confirmed
the shooters, locations, and times.

653
00:25:42,541 --> 00:25:44,000
Something's not clicking

654
00:25:44,001 --> 00:25:46,252
because the culprit
has no choice but to lie,

655
00:25:46,253 --> 00:25:48,463
- so that's what they're doing.
- Right.

656
00:25:48,464 --> 00:25:50,882
[Mr. T] And we believed them,
which is why it's not making sense.

657
00:25:50,883 --> 00:25:53,177
And I think the liar is Ms. H.

658
00:25:53,677 --> 00:25:56,179
Mr. L was alive between the first
and second round of shots.

659
00:25:56,180 --> 00:25:59,265
And the gunshot at 00:25
was aimed at the cabinet.

660
00:25:59,266 --> 00:26:00,808
We know he was shot to death,

661
00:26:00,809 --> 00:26:03,770
so it had to be between the fourth
and fifth rounds of fire.

662
00:26:03,771 --> 00:26:05,898
Then it really must be me.

663
00:26:06,690 --> 00:26:09,442
[host] <i>The final round is over.</i>

664
00:26:09,443 --> 00:26:11,402
<i>Please make your closing arguments.</i>

665
00:26:11,403 --> 00:26:15,740
I was ruled out as a suspect
from the very start,

666
00:26:15,741 --> 00:26:17,325
so I'm really happy about that.

667
00:26:17,326 --> 00:26:20,578
I'm confident the shot was fired
from the inside

668
00:26:20,579 --> 00:26:25,124
because I doubt anyone could
aim accurately from such a distance.

669
00:26:25,125 --> 00:26:29,087
If the shooter was outside,
only the victim would know their location,

670
00:26:29,088 --> 00:26:30,464
but if the shooter was inside,

671
00:26:31,006 --> 00:26:34,092
they would very likely
run into someone while fleeing the scene.

672
00:26:34,093 --> 00:26:37,178
I don't think the shooter
would take that risk.

673
00:26:37,179 --> 00:26:38,430
I think it was Ms. H.

674
00:26:38,931 --> 00:26:40,848
We saw her lowering her gun
in the CCTV footage.

675
00:26:40,849 --> 00:26:44,393
She just couldn't get a clear shot
from the dining hall.

676
00:26:44,394 --> 00:26:48,106
So she sprinted to the tower,
killed him, and left.

677
00:26:48,107 --> 00:26:50,191
That's why the culprit is you.

678
00:26:50,192 --> 00:26:52,151
- [in English] Goodbye!
- [Ms. H, in Korean] Am I the killer?

679
00:26:52,152 --> 00:26:53,778
If we go by what Mr. T said,

680
00:26:53,779 --> 00:26:55,029
it has to be me or Mr. T.

681
00:26:55,030 --> 00:26:57,783
We both think the other did it.

682
00:26:58,367 --> 00:27:01,160
Our alibis our similar,
but one of us is the culprit?

683
00:27:01,161 --> 00:27:03,037
I don't think that adds up.

684
00:27:03,038 --> 00:27:04,748
I think Mr. X did it.

685
00:27:05,290 --> 00:27:09,044
I find it really suspicious
that he moved around so much.

686
00:27:09,545 --> 00:27:13,798
<i>And shooting four times in a row
is such a foolish thing to do.</i>

687
00:27:13,799 --> 00:27:17,802
Ms. H insists she shot into the air
because she was startled,

688
00:27:17,803 --> 00:27:19,387
but that's a lie.

689
00:27:19,388 --> 00:27:22,723
She fired the shot that killed Mr. L.

690
00:27:22,724 --> 00:27:24,976
I think that's the only
plausible explanation.

691
00:27:24,977 --> 00:27:26,395
Ms. H is the culprit.

692
00:27:29,189 --> 00:27:31,607
VOTING COMPLETE

693
00:27:31,608 --> 00:27:34,402
[host] <i>Here are the voting results.</i>

694
00:27:34,403 --> 00:27:35,862
<i>The MASTER got zero votes.</i>

695
00:27:35,863 --> 00:27:37,280
<i>Mr. P got zero votes.</i>

696
00:27:37,281 --> 00:27:38,948
<i>Mr. T got zero votes.</i>

697
00:27:38,949 --> 00:27:40,408
<i>Ms. H got two votes.</i>

698
00:27:40,409 --> 00:27:42,493
<i>Mr. X got three votes.</i>

699
00:27:42,494 --> 00:27:45,246
<i>Mr. X got the most votes.</i>

700
00:27:45,247 --> 00:27:46,664
- [exclaims]
- [Ms. H exclaims]

701
00:27:46,665 --> 00:27:48,208
You people are dense!

702
00:27:49,293 --> 00:27:54,088
[host] <i>The selected player shall open
the ending box bearing their number</i>

703
00:27:54,089 --> 00:27:57,758
<i>and read the ending scenario aloud.</i>

704
00:27:57,759 --> 00:27:59,469
I have a feeling it's not Mr. X.

705
00:28:00,095 --> 00:28:01,596
"He's a scapegoat."

706
00:28:01,597 --> 00:28:03,472
"You failed to catch the culprit."

707
00:28:03,473 --> 00:28:07,059
"The other members' key secrets
were kept hidden to the end."

708
00:28:07,060 --> 00:28:10,646
<i>"The escape plan, revolvers, and scapegoat
were decided from the start."</i>

709
00:28:10,647 --> 00:28:12,064
<i>"Someone has to take the fall."</i>

710
00:28:12,065 --> 00:28:14,275
<i>"Now, he gets what they meant by that."</i>

711
00:28:14,276 --> 00:28:16,110
<i>"Mr. X eventually gets arrested."</i>

712
00:28:16,111 --> 00:28:18,154
"The investigation record stated

713
00:28:18,155 --> 00:28:20,656
he was a low-level operative
who fired in a panic

714
00:28:20,657 --> 00:28:22,909
while trying to escape."

715
00:28:22,910 --> 00:28:24,785
"Mr. T quietly slipped away,

716
00:28:24,786 --> 00:28:26,747
with no one catching on
that he was the shooter…"

717
00:28:27,581 --> 00:28:30,000
THE CULPRIT WAS MR. T

718
00:28:41,845 --> 00:28:43,804
"With no one catching on
that he was the shooter…"

719
00:28:43,805 --> 00:28:45,682
[laughs]

720
00:28:47,935 --> 00:28:49,060
Ah, damn it.

721
00:28:49,061 --> 00:28:50,979
- She cursed! [laughs]
- [Mr. P laughing]

722
00:28:51,563 --> 00:28:53,857
IT JUST SLIPPED OUT

723
00:28:54,441 --> 00:28:55,900
I got chills.

724
00:28:55,901 --> 00:28:56,984
CHILLING

725
00:28:56,985 --> 00:29:00,112
[Mr. X] <i>"After securing part of the funds,
he fled overseas."</i>

726
00:29:00,113 --> 00:29:01,739
Mr. T fled overseas?

727
00:29:01,740 --> 00:29:03,199
Mr. Take-off.

728
00:29:03,200 --> 00:29:05,785
"Mr. L's identity was never revealed.

729
00:29:05,786 --> 00:29:08,371
<i>He watched it all play out
from a distance.</i>

730
00:29:08,372 --> 00:29:12,750
<i>After cutting loose one of their own,
he quietly planned his next move."</i>

731
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:14,127
[Mr. P] Gosh, what a scary guy.

732
00:29:14,628 --> 00:29:18,422
"Ms. H quickly got her cards in order."

733
00:29:18,423 --> 00:29:21,218
<i>"She didn't get to be a queen,
but she stayed in the game."</i>

734
00:29:23,303 --> 00:29:24,929
[Mr. T]
She wanted to become a female boss.

735
00:29:24,930 --> 00:29:26,097
"Mr. P's ending."

736
00:29:26,098 --> 00:29:28,349
"With Mr. X convicted as the culprit,

737
00:29:28,350 --> 00:29:31,645
<i>his ten-year undercover operation
was deemed a failure."</i>

738
00:29:33,146 --> 00:29:34,147
[gasps]

739
00:29:35,148 --> 00:29:37,900
[Mr. X] "The organization was exposed,
but the true masterminds got away."

740
00:29:37,901 --> 00:29:40,569
- Oh, you were an undercover cop.
- [Mr. P] I was undercover.

741
00:29:40,570 --> 00:29:43,614
My wife was a victim

742
00:29:43,615 --> 00:29:45,700
- of this kind of phishing scam…
- [gasps]

743
00:29:45,701 --> 00:29:47,202
…so I wanted to take you all down.

744
00:29:47,995 --> 00:29:50,287
I told you earlier that someone was lying.

745
00:29:50,288 --> 00:29:51,372
That was me.

746
00:29:51,373 --> 00:29:54,291
I said I missed because I got nervous.

747
00:29:54,292 --> 00:29:55,418
That was the lie.

748
00:29:55,419 --> 00:29:56,461
I didn't miss.

749
00:29:57,754 --> 00:29:59,672
Yeah, I told you it wasn't me!

750
00:29:59,673 --> 00:30:01,048
- What does it matter now?
- I mean,

751
00:30:01,049 --> 00:30:02,591
I couldn't confess that I was the killer.

752
00:30:02,592 --> 00:30:04,552
Hey, this is pretty major.

753
00:30:04,553 --> 00:30:05,803
Because this log is just

754
00:30:05,804 --> 00:30:08,305
the ledger of the money
we made from our scam.

755
00:30:08,306 --> 00:30:10,600
- That's all it is. You need to see this.
- Okay.

756
00:30:11,184 --> 00:30:13,394
Yeah, that's when I zoned out.

757
00:30:13,395 --> 00:30:14,562
It really doesn't say what I did.

758
00:30:14,563 --> 00:30:15,564
PRETENDED TO LACK INFO

759
00:30:16,148 --> 00:30:18,482
But as I said earlier, needing a formula

760
00:30:18,483 --> 00:30:20,151
as I'm such a lousy shot, I missed.

761
00:30:20,152 --> 00:30:21,694
We barely have any clues about Mr. T.

762
00:30:21,695 --> 00:30:22,738
[Mr. P] I know, Mr. T…

763
00:30:23,405 --> 00:30:25,614
THERE WAS A LOT OF CONCLUSIVE EVIDENCE

764
00:30:25,615 --> 00:30:27,908
Oh, I think I know what that is.

765
00:30:27,909 --> 00:30:28,993
[Ms. H] What's that?

766
00:30:28,994 --> 00:30:30,828
[the MASTER] It was some kind of formula.

767
00:30:30,829 --> 00:30:32,371
MR. T WAS IN A PICKLE

768
00:30:32,372 --> 00:30:35,249
I think Faker is on to me.

769
00:30:35,250 --> 00:30:37,543
He looked at me suspiciously.

770
00:30:37,544 --> 00:30:39,545
I thought I'd been caught for sure.

771
00:30:39,546 --> 00:30:42,214
I don't have a very good poker face.

772
00:30:42,215 --> 00:30:43,716
We didn't catch the culprit last time.

773
00:30:43,717 --> 00:30:45,092
- You don't need to today.
- Why not?

774
00:30:45,093 --> 00:30:46,886
- Because you're the culprit.
- Why me? [chuckles]

775
00:30:46,887 --> 00:30:48,262
You traitor. [chuckles]

776
00:30:48,263 --> 00:30:49,638
What are you on about?

777
00:30:49,639 --> 00:30:51,265
I thought I was caught,

778
00:30:51,266 --> 00:30:54,518
but I think my strategy
of putting the spotlight on Ms. H

779
00:30:54,519 --> 00:30:56,937
was a really effective move.

780
00:30:56,938 --> 00:30:58,230
Where did you shoot from, Ms. H?

781
00:30:58,231 --> 00:31:00,191
Why did you kill him, Ms. H?

782
00:31:00,192 --> 00:31:01,817
Why did you lie?

783
00:31:01,818 --> 00:31:04,195
Why am I the one under suspicion?

784
00:31:04,196 --> 00:31:05,654
[Mr. T laughs]

785
00:31:05,655 --> 00:31:07,156
[Mr. P] That's just how life is.

786
00:31:07,157 --> 00:31:09,492
He shared so many clues

787
00:31:09,493 --> 00:31:12,953
that it threw me off his tail.

788
00:31:12,954 --> 00:31:17,083
I was so sure
the shot was fired from inside

789
00:31:17,084 --> 00:31:19,960
that I ruled him out.

790
00:31:19,961 --> 00:31:23,465
I'm confident the shot was fired
from the inside.

791
00:31:24,049 --> 00:31:26,133
KNOWINGLY SHAKING HIS HEAD

792
00:31:26,134 --> 00:31:27,676
Mr. T played it well.

793
00:31:27,677 --> 00:31:30,096
We were in the same boat

794
00:31:30,097 --> 00:31:33,057
but he turned all the focus to me,
so fair play to him.

795
00:31:33,058 --> 00:31:34,683
I started doubting myself!

796
00:31:34,684 --> 00:31:36,853
That's how convincing his act was.

797
00:31:37,437 --> 00:31:38,562
You're so annoying.

798
00:31:38,563 --> 00:31:41,065
- You cleverly got away with it.
- [laughs]

799
00:31:41,066 --> 00:31:43,025
I dropped a lot of hints. I really did.

800
00:31:43,026 --> 00:31:44,986
I feel like we were so close.

801
00:31:45,570 --> 00:31:47,363
- This game is really hard.
- [Mr. P] It's so hard.

802
00:31:47,364 --> 00:31:50,032
I think this was the hardest one yet.

803
00:31:50,033 --> 00:31:51,367
Even though I'm the culprit, I thought,

804
00:31:51,368 --> 00:31:52,785
"Wait. Did someone else do it?"

805
00:31:52,786 --> 00:31:55,288
- [laughing]
- Seriously, I started doubting it was me.

806
00:31:55,997 --> 00:31:57,581
FINAL THOUGHTS

807
00:31:57,582 --> 00:31:59,583
It's such a fun program,

808
00:31:59,584 --> 00:32:02,128
and playing the game
with such smart, young people

809
00:32:02,129 --> 00:32:04,046
has made me feel 20 years younger.

810
00:32:04,047 --> 00:32:06,340
It was a really meaningful experience.

811
00:32:06,341 --> 00:32:08,635
I hope after watching the last episode,

812
00:32:09,511 --> 00:32:11,929
the takeaway will be

813
00:32:11,930 --> 00:32:13,597
that scammers don't get a happy ending.

814
00:32:13,598 --> 00:32:15,975
- We're all scammers, right?
- Yeah.

815
00:32:15,976 --> 00:32:17,686
I hope all scammers get locked up.

816
00:32:18,478 --> 00:32:20,479
I've never really played
board games before,

817
00:32:20,480 --> 00:32:23,691
especially a game like this one

818
00:32:23,692 --> 00:32:25,651
that's so immersive and high-quality.

819
00:32:25,652 --> 00:32:28,737
I had so much fun
that the time just flew by.

820
00:32:28,738 --> 00:32:32,992
And I really enjoyed getting to play
with such great people.

821
00:32:32,993 --> 00:32:37,037
I also really enjoyed
getting to play a board game like this.

822
00:32:37,038 --> 00:32:39,790
I was determined
to solve a lot of mysteries,

823
00:32:39,791 --> 00:32:41,625
so I'm a bit disappointed
I didn't do that well.

824
00:32:41,626 --> 00:32:45,713
But everyone really gave it their all,

825
00:32:45,714 --> 00:32:48,507
so I had a really fun time.

826
00:32:48,508 --> 00:32:50,634
I thought I was the best at this game,

827
00:32:50,635 --> 00:32:51,720
but…

828
00:32:52,762 --> 00:32:57,016
The more we find out,
the more I realize I'm the worst at it.

829
00:32:57,017 --> 00:33:00,144
It was an eye-opening experience for me.

830
00:33:00,145 --> 00:33:04,231
And it was an honor to play
with such distinguished people.

831
00:33:04,232 --> 00:33:05,524
Thank you.

832
00:33:05,525 --> 00:33:06,734
- Great job, everyone.
- All right.

833
00:33:06,735 --> 00:33:08,611
- Good job.
- Great job.

834
00:33:08,612 --> 00:33:10,447
- Good work.
- Good job.

835
00:33:10,947 --> 00:33:13,782
THE FULL STORY

836
00:33:13,783 --> 00:33:14,993
[♪ dramatic music playing]

837
00:33:15,660 --> 00:33:19,372
00:00, THE LABYRINTH PRISON DOORS OPEN

838
00:33:20,081 --> 00:33:21,333
[panting]

839
00:33:27,422 --> 00:33:30,091
00:10, MS. H ARRIVES AT THE STORAGE ROOM

840
00:33:37,057 --> 00:33:41,603
00:15, THE MASTER AND MR. L
SHOOT EACH OTHER, 1ST ROUND OF GUNSHOTS

841
00:33:47,400 --> 00:33:48,735
[panting]

842
00:33:49,611 --> 00:33:51,154
[gasps]

843
00:33:54,324 --> 00:33:55,992
00:21,
MR. X FIRES THE 2ND ROUND OF GUNSHOTS

844
00:34:00,121 --> 00:34:02,332
00:25,
MR. P FIRES THE 3RD ROUND OF GUNSHOTS

845
00:34:06,795 --> 00:34:11,341
00:26, THE MASTER ARRIVES
AT THE STORAGE ROOM

846
00:34:16,388 --> 00:34:21,726
00:30, MR. T AND MS. H
FIRE THE 4TH ROUND OF GUNSHOTS

847
00:34:24,688 --> 00:34:27,524
00:32, MR. X FINDS MR. L DEAD

848
00:34:28,441 --> 00:34:29,776
[Ms. H breathes shakily]

849
00:34:40,829 --> 00:34:43,915
00:55, ALL MEMBERS ARRIVE
AT THE CONTROL TOWER

850
00:35:11,985 --> 00:35:13,987
Translated by Hannah Og Nam
